2026-06-22 18:30:54,817 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: Our consortium proposes an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist municipal agents in their daily missions, improving the efficiency of administrative services and the quality of service rendered to users. The proposed solution will provide an intelligent assistance tool accessible from the agents' work environment, accompanying them in their administrative activities.

The solution will facilitate access to reliable and up-to-date information coming from internal procedures, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents. It will also assist with drafting administrative contents, such as answers to users, administrative letters, and syntheses of files, ensuring that the generated contents are adapted to the administrative context and compliant with quality requirements.

Our solution integrates a cloud-native architecture using EU-based cloud providers like OVHcloud or Scaleway, ensuring sovereignty and compliance with regulatory requirements. We will design a microservices-based system with API integration using REST, GraphQL, or SOAP protocols, depending on the client's existing systems. The system will be secured with encryption, authentication, and secrets management mechanisms.

To ensure high availability, we will implement auto-scaling, load balancing, and monitoring using tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack. Our containerization strategy utilizes Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm to ensure efficient deployment and management of the solution.

The proposed solution will also facilitate continuity of processing between agents and services by allowing sharing of relevant information, understanding of the context of an ongoing file, and effective resumption of processing by another agent.

In terms of regulatory compliance, our solution guarantees strict adherence to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). We ensure EU-only data hosting, prohibit transfers outside the EU, and protect sensitive data using encryption and anonymization if necessary. Our Data Protection Officer is appointed, and we have a standard Data Protection Agreement template available.

Our security posture includes multi-factor authentication using TOTP or hardware tokens (FIDO2), Privileged Access Management solutions like CyberArk Conjur or HashiCorp Vault, and network security architecture patterns such as Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth. We conduct annual penetration testing and post-major release testing to ensure the security of our solution.

We prioritize explicability and transparency in our solution, utilizing source citation (RAG grounding) and chain-of-thought display to provide insights into recommendations or proposals issued by the solution. Our confidence scoring feature identifies cases where the model is uncertain, triggering human validation.

Our proposed approach includes a pilot phase on a limited scope, followed by progressive generalization to the entirety of the services. We will provide accompaniment to change and training for agents, ensuring a smooth transition to the new solution.

In terms of budgetary constraints, our target gross margin percentage is 28%. We aim to optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected, ensuring compatibility with the local authority's budgetary capacities. Our pricing model takes into account the total budget allocated by the client, which is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years.

Our solution also addresses environmental concerns, proposing several sustainability measures to reduce energetic consumption and relying on low-carbon impact infrastructures. We partner with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, who use 100% renewable energy and have low power usage effectiveness (PUE) scores. Our carbon reporting capability, based on the GRI Standards, enables us to track and report on the carbon footprint of our solution.

In conclusion, our consortium's proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily missions, while ensuring regulatory compliance, security, and environmental sustainability. We are confident that our solution will improve the efficiency of administrative services and the quality of service rendered to users, aligning with the local authority's priorities and budgetary constraints.
